ionally impossible/unverified (uses native VARIANT compatibility unverified) and expected baseline to provide an implementation that compiles perhaps using `__VARINFO`.\n\nLet's inspect task metadata: assumptions say \"Native CODESYS compatibility and runtime type/array metadata access remain unverified; never silently replace it by a DINT-only interface.\" So benchmark acknowledges uncertainty. The required solution likely uses dynamic metadata and tests may be custom simulator that implements VARIANT arrays. Need produce plausible.\n\nCould call compile with generic code and see.\n\nLet's design supporting helper functions to handle array metadata:\n- DUT `TYPE ST_QueueBinding : STRUCT ... END_STRUCT` maybe not needed.\n- Functions to retrieve variant info might need `ANY` types. Supporting_objects list can define helper functions.\n\nMaybe there is a standard library function `__VARINFO` that can get array info via `VAR_INFO` fields. Let's formulate implementation using `__VARINFO` and inspect compile messages. We'll use one compile call for probing a lot of plausible fields, but code must be syntactically valid. We can include unreachable variable assignments? Compiler compiles all. Use each candidate field in separate assignment to local variables. That reveals which fields exist; unknown fields errors, but valid ones no error. But if `VAR_INFO` type unknown, all fail. We need exact type name. `__SYSTEM.VAR_INFO` likely. Could declare `infoBuffer : __SYSTEM.VAR_INFO;`. Maybe this will compile.\n\nLet's recall `__SYSTEM.TYPE_CLASS` enum member names:\n```\nTYPE_CLASS.BOOL, BIT, BYTE, WORD, DWORD, LWORD, SINT, INT, DINT, LINT, USINT, UINT, UDINT, ULINT, REAL, LREAL, TIME, DATE, ...\n```\nMaybe not needed for initial.\n\nMaybe use `__VARINFO` return without declaring type:\n```\nIF __VARINFO(buffer).TypeClass = __SYSTEM.TYPE_CLASS.TYPE_ARRAY THEN\n...\n```\nCan the operator directly access fields? In ST, function results of struct type can access fields: `__VARINF